Author:     ba2-grid <ba2-grid@localhost>
AuthorDate: Mon Sep 21 05:53:47 2026 +0000
Commit:     ba2-grid <ba2-grid@localhost>
CommitDate: Mon Sep 21 05:53:47 2026 +0000

    fix(optimizer): a stalled trial no longer kills the job - score STALLED_SENTINEL, respawn the slot
    
    One wedged genome killed a 16-job matrix at job 1/16 (2026-09-20 21:54Z): the local pool stall
    guard raised TimeoutError and the whole run stopped, then sat dead 7.5h (detached Popen, no
    auto-restart).
    
    - _SlotPools.abandon_slot: terminate the wedged slot worker and respawn it WITHOUT waiting
      (_recycle_pool shutdown(wait=True) would block on the very worker being abandoned).
    - _local_execute_jobs: on a stall, score each pending individual at STALLED_SENTINEL, respawn its
      slot, log loudly, and CONTINUE instead of raising.
    - STALLED_SENTINEL = -3.0e9: distinct from the other sentinels so the frequency stays countable in
      all_results (operator ask); ranked below WIPED_OUT because a wedge is not a genome measurement.
    - batch_fitness: a stalled individual is memoized (so the same wedge cannot burn another timeout
      every generation) and RECORDED in all_results.
    - tests: test_local_pool_stall_recovery.py pins the ordering, the no-wait recovery (wedged worker
      really terminated) and the absence of the raise. TEST_APP_VERSION 0064 -> 0065.

